WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.567 --> 00:00:04.267
-Donald Trump was intimately
involved in plans to seize

00:00:04.267 --> 00:00:06.567
voting machines and stay in
power in the waning days

00:00:06.567 --> 00:00:07.801
of his presidency.

00:00:07.801 --> 00:00:10.100
Also, and I'm sure this is just
a coincidence,

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:11.901
a bunch of his white House
records were shredded

00:00:11.901 --> 00:00:13.367
and had to be
taped back together.

00:00:13.367 --> 00:00:15.934
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:15.934 --> 00:00:18.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:19.934 --> 00:00:21.200
Look, you guys,
I don't want to

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.067
talk about Trump
and I shouldn't have to.

00:00:23.067 --> 00:00:24.868
Normally when someone stops
being president,

00:00:24.868 --> 00:00:27.934
they go away and then later they
open their library

00:00:27.934 --> 00:00:29.901
and you say, "Damn, he got old."
and that's it.

00:00:30.701 --> 00:00:32.300
But Trump never went away for a
second.

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:34.400
So we here at "Late Night"
are on the coo-b.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:37.100
we've spent the last year or so
chronicling the brazen

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:39.200
criminality of Trump and his
weirdo henchmen

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.067
who tried to over throw American
democracy

00:00:41.067 --> 00:00:44.400
and are almost certainly gonna
try to do it again in 2024

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:45.567
as we call them the...

00:00:47.367 --> 00:00:49.133
[ Laughter ]

00:00:49.133 --> 00:00:51.300
Of one of them, God forbid,
ever buys a Cadillac

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:52.834
we'll have to
start calling them the...

00:00:54.434 --> 00:00:55.634
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.634 --> 00:00:57.100
But the point is we can't just
forget that Trump

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:59.200
and his movement tried to
overthrow democracy.

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.667
And they are, as we speak,
actively laying

00:01:01.667 --> 00:01:02.868
the ground work to do it again.

00:01:02.868 --> 00:01:05.434
Believe me,
I desperately wish he'd vanish

00:01:05.434 --> 00:01:06.734
and we'd never hear from him
again,

00:01:06.734 --> 00:01:07.868
but that's clearly not the case.

00:01:07.868 --> 00:01:10.167
He keeps hinting that he's gonna
run in 2024.

00:01:10.167 --> 00:01:12.701
And as nightmarish as it is to
even contemplate it

00:01:12.701 --> 00:01:14.634
there's a good chance he's gonna
be the Republican nominee.

00:01:14.634 --> 00:01:17.000
We have to be clear-eyed about
his criminality.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:18.734
Now some of you doubters out
there might be saying

00:01:18.734 --> 00:01:21.701
"Not so fast Ron DeSantis
looking pretty formidable

00:01:21.701 --> 00:01:23.634
and I'm sure he will continue to
look that way,

00:01:23.634 --> 00:01:26.200
until he gets on stage with
Donald Trump.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:28.701
because he's just doing a knock
off impression of Trump

00:01:28.701 --> 00:01:30.968
And given the choice, people
always choose the real thing.

00:01:30.968 --> 00:01:33.367
I mean, who do you think would
win a battle of the bands --

00:01:33.367 --> 00:01:36.601
U2 or four unknowns from Dublin
doing U2 covers?

00:01:36.601 --> 00:01:37.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.901 --> 00:01:42.667
One more time for U2,
now make some noise for Us Also!

00:01:42.667 --> 00:01:46.167
[ Irish accent ] Uh, we probably
should've gone first.

00:01:46.167 --> 00:01:49.067
[ Normal voice ]
Yeah, even their Irish accents
are gonna be bad.

00:01:49.067 --> 00:01:51.434
Point is, Trump won't go away
and he might run again.

00:01:51.434 --> 00:01:53.133
And if he does,
he'll almost certainly try to

00:01:53.133 --> 00:01:56.334
finish what he started with his
attempted coup last time around.

00:01:56.334 --> 00:01:58.501
And the GOP's either actively
complicit

00:01:58.501 --> 00:02:00.901
in that slow-moving coup
or ignoring it

00:02:00.901 --> 00:02:03.234
so they can spend their time
throwing a racist temper tantrum

00:02:03.234 --> 00:02:05.901
over President Biden's pledge to
appoint a black woman

00:02:05.901 --> 00:02:07.634
as the Supreme Court justice.

00:02:07.634 --> 00:02:09.400
-Joe Biden's promise to choose
a black woman

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:11.634
as his Supreme Court nominee
is divisive.

00:02:11.634 --> 00:02:12.801
It's un-American.

00:02:12.801 --> 00:02:16.200
Racial preferences,
sexual preferences.

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:17.601
First of all it's illegal.

00:02:17.601 --> 00:02:21.667
-The way that the president has
handled this nomination

00:02:21.667 --> 00:02:23.901
has been clumsy at best.

00:02:23.901 --> 00:02:28.334
It adds to the further
perception that the Court

00:02:28.334 --> 00:02:31.667
is a political institution like
Congress.

00:02:31.667 --> 00:02:34.400
-The fact that he's willing to
make a promise at the outset

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:37.567
that it must be a black woman,
I gotta say, that's offensive.

00:02:37.567 --> 00:02:38.868
-Right. Right if --

00:02:38.868 --> 00:02:42.400
-Black women are what,
6% of the U.S. population?

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:45.901
He's saying to 94% of Americans,
"I don't give a damn about you.

00:02:45.901 --> 00:02:47.267
You are ineligible.

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:51.467
He's saying, "If you're a white
guy, tough luck."

00:02:51.467 --> 00:02:53.434
If you're a white woman tough
luck, you don't qualify."

00:02:53.434 --> 00:02:55.734
-Hey, man, what the [bleep] you
talking about?

00:02:55.734 --> 00:02:59.133
There have been more white guys
on the Supreme Court

00:02:59.133 --> 00:03:03.367
than there are at a Patagonia
clearance sale in Connecticut.

00:03:03.367 --> 00:03:06.067
Normally to see that many white
guys on the bench,

00:03:06.067 --> 00:03:09.067
you'd have to watch
March Madness.

00:03:09.067 --> 00:03:11.234
Out of 115 Supreme Court
justices,

00:03:11.234 --> 00:03:13.200
108 have been white men.

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:15.667
You're a white guy who went to
an Ivy League school

00:03:15.667 --> 00:03:18.000
they call you in the day before
graduation and say

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:19.968
"Alright, you want to write for
'The Simpsons'

00:03:19.968 --> 00:03:21.133
or be on the Supreme Court?"

00:03:21.133 --> 00:03:22.667
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.667 --> 00:03:25.133
White guys complaining about not
getting on the Supreme Court are

00:03:25.133 --> 00:03:28.200
like Patriots fans complaining
about the last three years.

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:30.901
"When's it gonna be our time?"

00:03:30.901 --> 00:03:32.701
Anyway, back to the...

00:03:33.634 --> 00:03:36.701
Personally, I might be less
focused on the various

00:03:36.701 --> 00:03:38.701
investigations into Trump,
if Trump himself

00:03:38.701 --> 00:03:39.868
were less focused on them.

00:03:39.868 --> 00:03:41.367
I mean, he talks about them
non-stop.

00:03:41.367 --> 00:03:44.133
And the New York Times reporter,
Maggie Haberman, wrote recently

00:03:44.133 --> 00:03:46.834
that Trump's aides have always
signaled that if

00:03:46.834 --> 00:03:48.601
the investigations progressed,

00:03:48.601 --> 00:03:50.200
that he would
run for president again.

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:52.501
Trump is so obsessed with the
various investigations

00:03:52.501 --> 00:03:55.000
into his personal and business
affairs he ranted about them,

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:57.067
at length,
at one of his truckless

00:03:57.067 --> 00:03:59.200
monster truck rallies
over the weekend.

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:02.601
-They are viciously and
unconstitutionally using

00:04:02.601 --> 00:04:06.200
the federal, local, and state
governments to prosecute

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:10.133
and silence politicians like me.

00:04:10.133 --> 00:04:12.834
For years, they've been going
after my company.

00:04:12.834 --> 00:04:15.667
Many years,
using every trick in the book

00:04:15.667 --> 00:04:20.701
in an attempt to literally,
if they can, put me in jail.

00:04:20.701 --> 00:04:26.167
They've subpoenaed more than
9 million pages, big company,

00:04:26.167 --> 00:04:27.467
of documents.

00:04:27.467 --> 00:04:30.534
And virtually every deal I've
ever done hoping to find

00:04:30.534 --> 00:04:36.167
a mistake, an error, misspelled
words, a comma out of place.

00:04:36.167 --> 00:04:38.767
Or anything else
that they can find

00:04:38.767 --> 00:04:40.934
that might be just a little bit
wrong.

00:04:40.934 --> 00:04:43.834
All these "never Trump-ers"
working full-time

00:04:43.834 --> 00:04:47.033
in the prosecutors office
to get Trump

00:04:47.033 --> 00:04:50.868
because they couldn't do it
before because they had nothing

00:04:50.868 --> 00:04:52.534
after all these years, can you
believe it?

00:04:52.534 --> 00:04:56.367
How do you like my life?
You think I have a good time?

00:04:56.367 --> 00:04:58.868
Actually, I guess
there's something going on

00:04:58.868 --> 00:05:00.367
because I do have a good time.

00:05:00.367 --> 00:05:04.534
-I'm not sure you do have
a good life.

00:05:04.534 --> 00:05:07.834
If you did, I don't think you'd
have to drag your supporters out

00:05:07.834 --> 00:05:09.901
twice a week to clap for you
like some kind of

00:05:09.901 --> 00:05:11.400
geriatric Tinker Bell.

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:13.767
[ As Trump ] Folks, if you clap
for me, I'll come back to life

00:05:13.767 --> 00:05:16.667
and we'll put Hillary in jail
for the computer thing.

00:05:16.667 --> 00:05:19.701
If you only believe.

00:05:19.701 --> 00:05:21.000
[ Normal voice ] You sound like
the guy who insists

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:23.400
he has a great marriage,
but also thinks we should

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:25.734
start doing poker night twice a
week.

00:05:25.734 --> 00:05:27.934
But, yes, I agree,
there's something going on.

00:05:27.934 --> 00:05:30.934
In fact, I guess that's the
official medical diagnosis

00:05:30.934 --> 00:05:32.801
from looking at a CAT scan
of your brain.

00:05:32.801 --> 00:05:36.033
Well, Mr. Trump, I've looked
over the images and there's no

00:05:36.033 --> 00:05:38.234
easy way to say this,
there's something going on.

00:05:38.234 --> 00:05:39.934
My last doctor didn't see
anything.

00:05:39.934 --> 00:05:43.434
Is that the same doctor who said
you were in great shape?

00:05:43.434 --> 00:05:46.133
What's your point?
Oh, [bleep].

00:05:46.133 --> 00:05:47.200
[ Laughter ]

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:48.667
Also, could we go back to this?

00:05:48.667 --> 00:05:54.000
-They've subpoenaed more than
9 million pages, big company,

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:55.300
of documents.

00:05:55.300 --> 00:05:58.334
And virtually every deal I've
ever done hoping to find

00:05:58.334 --> 00:06:04.033
a mistake, an error, misspelled
words, a comma out of place.

00:06:04.033 --> 00:06:06.567
-I don't think they need to hope
to find a misspelling

00:06:06.567 --> 00:06:08.200
or a comma outta place.

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:10.734
Looking for misspellings in a
Trump document is like

00:06:10.734 --> 00:06:14.601
looking for Waldo in a book
called "Only Waldos."

00:06:14.601 --> 00:06:17.634
Most of your tweets look like
you typed them left-handed

00:06:17.634 --> 00:06:20.300
in the middle of a sword fight.

00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:22.434
In fact, Trump's paranoia about
what he calls mistakes

00:06:22.434 --> 00:06:24.467
in his personal and professional
documents apparently

00:06:24.467 --> 00:06:26.434
manifested itself
in very real ways,

00:06:26.434 --> 00:06:29.167
because when the National
Archives handed over a trove

00:06:29.167 --> 00:06:31.234
of documents from the Trump
White House to the committee

00:06:31.234 --> 00:06:33.901
investigating the January 6th
insurrection,

00:06:33.901 --> 00:06:37.133
some of them had apparently been
torn up and taped back together.

00:06:37.133 --> 00:06:39.033
-The National Archives,
in a statement,

00:06:39.033 --> 00:06:42.133
confirming that some of the
documents that they received

00:06:42.133 --> 00:06:44.200
from the Trump White House that
were of interest

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:46.501
in the January 6th select
committee

00:06:46.501 --> 00:06:48.834
came to them ripped up,
shredded up.

00:06:48.834 --> 00:06:51.501
And they were forced to tape
them back up

00:06:51.501 --> 00:06:54.467
before they were given to the
January 6th select committee.

00:06:54.467 --> 00:06:57.534
Now, we don't know exactly which
documents these are,

00:06:57.534 --> 00:06:59.767
but we do know that the former
President Donald Trump

00:06:59.767 --> 00:07:02.534
has a habit of tearing up
documents,

00:07:02.534 --> 00:07:04.834
that, in some cases,
former White House staffers

00:07:04.834 --> 00:07:06.534
had to tape together.

00:07:06.534 --> 00:07:09.267
This was a practice that went
back to as late as 2018.

00:07:09.267 --> 00:07:11.601
So, it is significant that this
was something that continued

00:07:11.601 --> 00:07:13.701
right up until the end of the
Trump administration.

00:07:13.701 --> 00:07:16.033
-It doesn't surprise me that
Trump treated official

00:07:16.033 --> 00:07:18.367
presidential records the way
the rest of us treat

00:07:18.367 --> 00:07:21.567
credit card offers from Discover
or the way I treat

00:07:21.567 --> 00:07:23.701
autograph requests from my
wife's niece.

00:07:23.701 --> 00:07:26.000
Get lost, Becky!
[ Laughter ]

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:28.601
She puts them on eBay
and then complains to me

00:07:28.601 --> 00:07:30.968
when they don't get any bids --
she's no angel.

00:07:30.968 --> 00:07:33.834
[ Laughter ]

00:07:33.834 --> 00:07:36.133
I would say shredding documents
is an obvious sign

00:07:36.133 --> 00:07:38.567
of someone's guilt, but I'm sure
Trump does it with everything.

00:07:38.567 --> 00:07:41.534
[ As Trump ] That's another
3-under round for Donald Trump.

00:07:41.534 --> 00:07:44.033
Tear this up for me
into a million pieces.

00:07:44.033 --> 00:07:45.534
[ Normal voice ] Also, let's all
spare a thought

00:07:45.534 --> 00:07:47.767
to the federal employee who had
to tape all of Donald Trump's

00:07:47.767 --> 00:07:49.467
presidential records back
together,

00:07:49.467 --> 00:07:53.000
just getting Ziploc after Ziploc
full of confetti

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:55.000
soaked in hand sweat and then
trying to figure out

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:58.000
which words to put together to
form sentences.

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:00.567
Piecing together Trump's notes
is like fishing

00:08:00.567 --> 00:08:03.367
a bunch of magnetic poetry out
of a garbage disposal.

00:08:03.367 --> 00:08:05.734
But it turns out Trump had good
reason to rip up the evidence to

00:08:05.734 --> 00:08:07.300
all the crazy [bleep] he did in
the White House.

00:08:07.300 --> 00:08:10.334
Every day we find out more about
just how close he came to

00:08:10.334 --> 00:08:11.701
pulling off a full-blown coup.

00:08:11.701 --> 00:08:13.868
Recently we learned that his
administration has drafted

00:08:13.868 --> 00:08:16.133
several executive orders to
seize voting machines

00:08:16.133 --> 00:08:18.100
And then this week,
we learned that Trump

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:21.601
was directly and personally
involved in those discussions.

00:08:21.601 --> 00:08:24.534
-The New York Times reporting
that 6 weeks after the 2020

00:08:24.534 --> 00:08:27.734
race, which he lost, Mr. Trump
directed his attorney

00:08:27.734 --> 00:08:30.667
Rudy Giuliani to ask the
Department of Homeland Security

00:08:30.667 --> 00:08:34.200
if it could legally take control
of voting machines

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:35.667
in key swing states.

00:08:35.667 --> 00:08:39.501
-Donald Trump's advisors drafted
more than one executive order to

00:08:39.501 --> 00:08:42.434
seize voting machines
during the former president's

00:08:42.434 --> 00:08:43.601
final weeks in office.

00:08:43.601 --> 00:08:45.334
There was one order for the
Pentagon --

00:08:45.334 --> 00:08:48.767
we had known about that --
but overnight CNN reporting on

00:08:48.767 --> 00:08:51.300
another for Homeland Security.

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:54.634
-Trump also tried to persuade
state law makers in Michigan

00:08:54.634 --> 00:08:57.434
and Pennsylvania to use local
law enforcement

00:08:57.434 --> 00:08:59.434
to take control of the voting
machines in those states

00:08:59.434 --> 00:09:01.467
but they also refused to do so.

00:09:01.467 --> 00:09:04.167
Trump then moved onto the
military.

00:09:04.167 --> 00:09:06.834
-Man, Trump tried everything --
Justice Department,

00:09:06.834 --> 00:09:09.100
Homeland Security,
swing state law makers,

00:09:09.100 --> 00:09:10.634
even Rudy Giuliani.

00:09:10.634 --> 00:09:13.701
of all people, I can't believe,
and yet, also I can believe

00:09:13.701 --> 00:09:16.467
that he had Rudy call the
Department of Homeland Security.

00:09:16.467 --> 00:09:17.901
Although, who knows with Rudy.

00:09:17.901 --> 00:09:20.434
It could've been a butt dial,
which he's done before for real.

00:09:20.434 --> 00:09:24.367
In 2019 Rudy butt-dialed an NBC
reporter.

00:09:24.367 --> 00:09:27.100
And it makes sense because Rudy
always looks like he just

00:09:27.100 --> 00:09:29.234
sat on his phone

00:09:29.234 --> 00:09:31.267
and accidentally made an
emergency call.

00:09:31.267 --> 00:09:33.334
9-1-1, what's your emergency?

00:09:33.334 --> 00:09:34.968
There's a voice coming from my
pants.

00:09:34.968 --> 00:09:37.167
Sir, sir that's me.

00:09:37.167 --> 00:09:40.767
My, my penis?

00:09:40.767 --> 00:09:44.501
One of the terrifying reasons
Trump's coup didn't work

00:09:44.501 --> 00:09:46.100
is that Trump is a lazy moron.

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:47.801
He tried every avenue
he could think of

00:09:47.801 --> 00:09:49.167
and he almost pulled it off.

00:09:49.167 --> 00:09:50.701
if he'd been more disciplined
or more diligent,

00:09:50.701 --> 00:09:52.100
he probably could've done it.

00:09:52.100 --> 00:09:53.767
But that's why we can't just
move on and forget about it

00:09:53.767 --> 00:09:56.200
because either Trump or someone
even more ruthless

00:09:56.200 --> 00:09:58.801
will come along and try it again
in 2024.

00:09:58.801 --> 00:10:00.868
And the GOP is already laying
the groundwork

00:10:00.868 --> 00:10:02.234
for the next coup as we speak.

00:10:02.234 --> 00:10:04.701
Meanwhile, Trump is --
-Using every trick in the book.

